# Realtime & Notifications

## Socket lifecycle

The app should:
- connect after authentication
- reconnect safely
- disconnect on logout
- handle app background/foreground transitions appropriately
- avoid duplicate listeners

Register each event listener once per lifecycle.

## Realtime events

Typical events:
```text
message:new
message:read
message:reaction
correction:created
typing:start
typing:stop
presence:updated
```

Use server events as authoritative.

## Push notifications

Push can cover:
- new messages
- connection requests
- accepted connections
- corrections
- learning reminders
- security events

Respect notification settings.

Do not place sensitive private message contents into push payloads unless the product explicitly supports it and privacy requirements are satisfied.

## Badge counts

Keep badge state consistent with server state where possible.
Do not permanently increment badges on duplicate realtime/push deliveries.
